    "campaign": {
      "revision": "osat-cold-zh-Hans-v1-locale-style",
      "instructions": "Single square cold advertisement, not a carousel. Preserve the supplied official Digiwin logo exactly once, no extra DIGIWIN word. Transfer only frozen R2 visual grammar: bright white and pale blue material world, deep navy and vivid blue large type, neutral daylight, soft grounded shadows, photographic tactile depth and relationships integrated into the scene. Do not transfer reference copy, props, exact scene or card numbers. NO sequence number or swipe instruction. Hierarchy: official logo and the exact role line at top, then category readable at 332px feed width, then dominant readable headline, readable support and a grounded narrative scene below. The headline is the main visual anchor, category and ERP role text need large comfortable font size rather than tiny header labels. Artwork should have no tiny text. Print only reviewed artwork text and the official brand mark, no added labels, no reference headings, no punctuation added to the role line. No metrics, result guarantees, customer logo, fabricated record values or screens, faces or glowing technology decoration. Preserve Simplified Chinese glyphs and exact supplied punctuation. Never mix scripts or use pseudo-Chinese. Use ASCII parentheses for approved acronym definitions to remain compatible with the frozen gate; do not normalize other punctuation. Review Chinese punctuation at line starts/ends and mixed Latin terms at 333px; reduce scene area before shrinking type.\nLOCALE: zh-Hans. Print only supplied Simplified Chinese artwork text. Professional operational Chinese: clear reconciliation objects and responsible team, concise question and practical next step. Use supplied mainland terminology, not word-for-word Vietnamese syntax. No assumptions about national personality, certification or guaranteed results. Keep original scene and narrative order. Preserve Simplified Chinese glyphs and exact supplied punctuation. Never mix scripts or use pseudo-Chinese. Use ASCII parentheses for approved acronym definitions to remain compatible with the frozen gate; do not normalize other punctuation. Review Chinese punctuation at line starts/ends and mixed Latin terms at 333px; reduce scene area before shrinking type."
    }
